{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-L8-panel-screens-2-01","date":"2026-11-22","lens":"8","surface":"panel","area":"panel/screens-2","refs":["F-panel-311","F-panel-303"],"severity":"S2","title":"Each 'Well done' sent from Training progress uses one of the gym's 10 member messages a day, with no warning","what":"Every 'Well done' or 'How's it going' sent from the Training progress page counts as a full member message. The gym can send only 10 a day. An owner who cheers 10 members has used up the day, and a later 'gym closed today' notice is refused. The Training progress page never says that cheers use the daily limit or how many are left.","expected":"Cheers to one member do not eat the gym's daily notice limit, or the page shows how many messages are left today before the owner sends one.","evidence":["apps/dashboard/src/crm/ui/screens/MyMembers.tsx:163-170","apps/dashboard/src/crm/ui/screens/MyMembers.tsx:243","supabase/migrations/0042_message_calm.sql:97-98","apps/dashboard/src/crm/shop/messages.ts:120-121","apps/dashboard/src/crm/shop/messages.ts:296-297"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"cheers-share-gym-daily-message-cap","who":"owners","how_often":"on busy days when the owner cheers many members","fix_line":"Give one-to-one cheers their own allowance, or show the messages left today on the Training progress page","fix_size":"small","needs_him":true,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
